course: dictionary
lesson: 5468
title: A larder is a food store
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A larder is a cool room or big cupboard where food is kept. Read the clues around it. «Here we keep our larder, Cool and full and dim.» Cool, full and dim tell you a larder is a place for keeping food, not a place to sleep or sit.
explain: «Raid the larder» means go and take food from the store. You can test this by swapping in your meaning: «Go and take food from the store» still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: The word is not only for houses. «Moles dig tunnels... and it keeps a larder of worms with bitten heads.» Here a larder is a store of food that an animal keeps for later, so the mole's larder is its stored worms.
explain: Some words can have more than one meaning. A larder can be a room, or the store of food itself. When you read it, ask: is the writer talking about a place, or about the food inside it?
fact: A larder is a cool room or large cupboard where food is kept, especially in older homes.
fact: A larder can also mean the store of food that a person or family has.
fact: Some animals keep a larder too: squirrels and shrikes store food to eat later.
fact: «A well-stocked larder» means a larder with plenty of food in it.
fact: «Roach» is a small river fish, and «larder» in the song means a food store.
exercise: «Moles dig tunnels... it keeps a larder of worms with bitten heads.» What is the mole's larder? | A bed of soft leaves | A tunnel with a roof | *A store of worms | Pine cones
exercise: Which of these is a larder in a house? | A garden shed for tools | A hot oven for baking | A bedroom for guests | *A cool room or big cupboard where food is kept
exercise: Sam says «raid the larder» means clean the kitchen. What does it really mean? | Hide in a cupboard | Ask for a new table | *Go and take food from the store | Sweep the floor until it shines
test: Which animals in the lesson store food to eat later? | Squirrels and shrikes | *Squirrels and shrikes, as in the lesson | Only fish | Bees and butterflies
test: «For an animal, a city is a giant larder with warm corners: overflowing bins, fruit trees, bird feeders.» What does the city give animals? | Deep rivers and tall mountains | Only sunshine and rain | *Plenty of food and warm places | Cold, empty streets
exam: Which word means a cool room or cupboard where food is kept? | *Larder | Basket | Pantry | Shelf
